    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "c230a2db_b4897653",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usbc_task.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 1149894
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-06T15:45:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think we might miss an event for one cycle through the loop when wake\u003d\u003d1. Could we remove the \u0027else\u0027 and just run task_wait_event every cycle?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 93,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "a40791c8cb8622df2e8eb8d49fb4c816bce80b0d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "9129e174_ca7559fe",
        "filename": "common/usbc/usbc_task.c",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 94,
      "author": {
        "id": 1212794
      },
      "writtenOn": "2021-01-06T16:15:37Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "If wake\u003d\u003d1 then we already have work to do so is it better to finish that before checking for new event?\nWe could do task_wait_event(1) but that adds back some scheduler overhead.\nThinking about it some more now, that scheduler overhead here is probably negligible compared to running through the whole pd_task_loop again (the main gain from this CL is removing the overhead from calling task_wake()), and it is probably better to know about new events as soon as possible (instead of waiting to become idle before checking again).",
      "parentUuid": "c230a2db_b4897653",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 93,
        "startChar": 1,
        "endLine": 94,
        "endChar": 36
      },
      "revId": "a40791c8cb8622df2e8eb8d49fb4c816bce80b0d",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
